WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.800
- Welcome, everyone.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.800
I am really excited to welcome
Dr. Andrew Harris here today,

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.980
not least because his work
on Angkorian archeology

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.590
resonates with the important

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.710
work of our recently
departed dear colleague,

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.850
the archeologists Michael Cole,

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.440
who as many of you know,

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.723
has had a long history of important work

00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:30.750
into Angkorian archeology.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.110
And also as many of you know,

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:33.850
here at Yale we have a long-standing

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.700
scholarly engagement with Cambodia

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.310
under the stewardship of
my wonderful colleague,

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:41.910
Ben Kiernan in the history department.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.220
I'm also excited for the
ways that Andrew's work

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.050
might intersect with a burgeoning

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.620
interest in Buddhist studies here at Yale,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.070
which is guided by another
of my wonderful colleagues,

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.310
one, Tsu Kim,

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.313
