00:32:49.070 --> 00:32:50.830
fulfill the same virtual functions,

00:32:50.830 --> 00:32:52.590
but evidently those
structures near the center

00:32:52.590 --> 00:32:54.960
had the capacity to host
larger congregations

00:32:54.960 --> 00:32:56.350
and feature elegantly carved,

00:32:56.350 --> 00:32:59.048
likely quarried sandstone substructures.

00:32:59.048 --> 00:33:01.650
Epigrapher (indistinct) for example,

00:33:01.650 --> 00:33:03.680
suggested that monks
may have been ordained

00:33:03.680 --> 00:33:05.880
at more prominent Preah Vihear complexes

00:33:05.880 --> 00:33:07.300
and built their own prayer halls,

00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:10.410
where they lived with the
resources at their disposal.

00:33:10.410 --> 00:33:12.260
And their Preah Vihear's
similar to temple's

00:33:12.260 --> 00:33:14.960
served as satellites of
political religious authority

00:33:14.960 --> 00:33:16.904
for the regions in which
they were constructed.

00:33:16.904 --> 00:33:19.010
The use of recycled stone to build these

00:33:19.010 --> 00:33:22.030
smaller structures on the
periphery is notably abundant,

00:33:22.030 --> 00:33:23.610
as well stressing the inequality

00:33:23.610 --> 00:33:25.060
between monastic populations.

00:33:26.560 --> 00:33:28.900
Also key to upholding political
and religious authority

00:33:28.900 --> 00:33:31.280
across the Angkorian
Empire was the standardized

00:33:31.280 --> 00:33:33.890
replication of a central
religious sanctuary.

00:33:33.890 --> 00:33:35.700
One wish in our understanding in Mandala

00:33:35.700 --> 00:33:38.320
unified the elites of the
state under a common worldview

00:33:38.320 --> 00:33:39.930
and thus an imperial rule,

00:33:39.930 --> 00:33:41.560
which strengthened the
periphery of the state

00:33:41.560 --> 00:33:43.150
in relation to the center.

00:33:43.150 --> 00:33:45.760
Although no evidence has
thus far been identified

00:33:45.760 --> 00:33:48.629
to suggest a central
monastic help within Angkor.

00:33:48.629 --> 00:33:50.370
The great monastery of Tep Pranam,

00:33:50.370 --> 00:33:53.110
Angkor's largest Buddhist
terrace complex is the most

00:33:53.110 --> 00:33:55.270
probable candidate to fulfill this role

00:33:55.270 --> 00:33:57.210
based on existing archeological evidence.

00:33:57.210 --> 00:34:00.680
Tep pranam which is found
directly north of the royal palace

00:34:00.680 --> 00:34:02.960
was continuously expanded
by unknown factions

00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:05.150
under unknown monarchs
and no inscription exists

00:34:05.150 --> 00:34:07.670
to dedicate to it's initial foundation.

00:34:07.670 --> 00:34:10.823
However, an inscription
was found there in 1908,

00:34:11.720 --> 00:34:13.620
that had been moved from a Buddhist ashram

00:34:13.620 --> 00:34:15.010
dedicated by the 9th century

00:34:15.010 --> 00:34:17.900
king Jayavarman the first at
least five centuries earlier,

00:34:17.900 --> 00:34:19.740
and Tep Pranam was actually thought

00:34:19.740 --> 00:34:23.480
to be the site of an early Hindu building.

00:34:23.480 --> 00:34:25.730
The same inscription and
its accompanying ashram

00:34:25.730 --> 00:34:27.780
was also rededicated by the 11th century

00:34:27.780 --> 00:34:29.350
king Jayavarman the first,

00:34:29.350 --> 00:34:32.910
who despite constructing a
temple mountain was a Buddhist.

00:34:32.910 --> 00:34:35.470
The steelie clearly
was moved with purpose,

00:34:35.470 --> 00:34:38.210
as other foundation steelies
unrelated to Buddhist

00:34:38.210 --> 00:34:39.700
entirely have been found at other

00:34:39.700 --> 00:34:42.503
Buddhist terrace complexes as deposits,

00:34:42.503 --> 00:34:44.820
and potentially signify Tep Pranam

00:34:44.820 --> 00:34:46.930
as an established royal sanctuary.

00:34:46.930 --> 00:34:50.770
The actual ashram, which
was identified fully

00:34:50.770 --> 00:34:53.060
in the early 2000s is found

00:34:53.060 --> 00:34:55.390
more than four miles
away and does not appear

00:34:55.390 --> 00:34:58.203
to have been used since it's
11th century rededication.

00:34:59.930 --> 00:35:01.230
Visually, if correct,

00:35:01.230 --> 00:35:03.130
and of course we need to excavate more

00:35:04.222 --> 00:35:05.528
to establish the specifics.

00:35:05.528 --> 00:35:06.361
There appears to be a clear aim

00:35:06.361 --> 00:35:08.140
by Angkor's Buddhist
populations and rulers

00:35:08.140 --> 00:35:09.770
to ensure a smooth transition between

00:35:09.770 --> 00:35:13.094
past and present principles
of religious space.

00:35:13.094 --> 00:35:14.867
But how did Angkorian populations deal

00:35:14.867 --> 00:35:16.947
with the overwhelming number of Hindu

00:35:16.947 --> 00:35:20.030
and Mahayana Buddhist
temples in their midst.

00:35:20.030 --> 00:35:21.850
Close to five centuries
of temple mountains

00:35:21.850 --> 00:35:23.880
are found within the capital central zone.

00:35:23.880 --> 00:35:25.590
Still, and it's not yet clear

00:35:25.590 --> 00:35:27.950
whether any temples were
demolished to build buildings

00:35:27.950 --> 00:35:29.900
or build monastic buildings despite

00:35:29.900 --> 00:35:32.070
the abundant use of recycled sand stone.

00:35:32.070 --> 00:35:34.920
But the original temple space
is a cellar holding a lingam,

00:35:34.920 --> 00:35:36.920
no longer exists at any of these tables.

00:35:38.060 --> 00:35:39.920
So how were these places reconciled

00:35:39.920 --> 00:35:41.040
with a new built environment,

00:35:41.040 --> 00:35:43.640
especially since a large
number of the temples

00:35:43.640 --> 00:35:45.490
were in fact converting?

00:35:45.490 --> 00:35:47.990
Well, first as Zhou Daguan described

00:35:47.990 --> 00:35:49.520
a period of religious pluralism

00:35:49.520 --> 00:35:52.230
followed both Jayavarman
eight's Hindu iconoclasm,

00:35:52.230 --> 00:35:54.090
and the institutionalization of Theravada

00:35:54.090 --> 00:35:55.640
in the late 13th century.

00:35:55.640 --> 00:35:58.110
So this may have not even
been an issue until the 14th,

00:35:58.110 --> 00:35:59.920
which marks the point
when many Preah Vihear

00:35:59.920 --> 00:36:02.070
were inhabited if not constructed.

00:36:02.070 --> 00:36:04.470
But as Preah Vihear space
began to become the predominant

00:36:04.470 --> 00:36:06.960
area of worship and Hindu practice,

00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:10.335
and, or worship and Hindu
practices were slowly phased out.

00:36:10.335 --> 00:36:12.930
Rather than demolishing these temples,

00:36:12.930 --> 00:36:15.010
they were transformed or negotiated.

00:36:15.010 --> 00:36:16.570
Only Lathum's live space,

00:36:16.570 --> 00:36:18.060
or Edward Soja's third space,

00:36:18.060 --> 00:36:19.780
provide key theoretical frameworks

00:36:19.780 --> 00:36:21.400
to understanding the types of processes

00:36:21.400 --> 00:36:23.320
embedded within converted temples

00:36:23.320 --> 00:36:25.230
and how conversions changed over time

00:36:25.230 --> 00:36:27.570
based on the perception
of ancient monuments.

00:36:27.570 --> 00:36:29.930
I also wanna importantly
knowledge that this research

00:36:29.930 --> 00:36:31.380
from an anthropological perspective

00:36:31.380 --> 00:36:32.530
was first undertaken by

00:36:32.530 --> 00:36:35.150
Dr. Ashley Thompson from SOAS,

00:36:35.150 --> 00:36:38.113
whose work was an important
inspiration for my own.

00:36:39.400 --> 00:36:41.370
One major indicator that
temples are converted

00:36:41.370 --> 00:36:43.850
was the installation of
a prescribed iconography,

00:36:43.850 --> 00:36:46.490
likely imported from contemporary
Thai Buddhist imagery,

00:36:46.490 --> 00:36:47.670
which is found represented in

00:36:47.670 --> 00:36:49.632
both standing statuary and beliefs.

00:36:49.632 --> 00:36:51.610
Each image intentionally depicts

00:36:51.610 --> 00:36:53.704
a specific episodes in
the life of the Buddha,

00:36:53.704 --> 00:36:56.700
the Parinirvana image on
the lower left, for example,

00:36:56.700 --> 00:36:58.422
illustrates the Buddha
breaking the life cycle

00:36:58.422 --> 00:37:01.470
and passing into Nirvana after his death.

00:37:01.470 --> 00:37:04.820
Whereas the earth touching
Buddha in the both on the right

00:37:05.970 --> 00:37:08.210
is constructed in reference

00:37:08.210 --> 00:37:10.097
to Buddhist defeat of the demon Mara,

00:37:10.097 --> 00:37:13.520
asking the earth to witness
it's victory through touch.

00:37:13.520 --> 00:37:15.990
These images are almost, almost constant,

00:37:15.990 --> 00:37:18.010
always constant across converted temples,

00:37:18.010 --> 00:37:19.640
and are far more uniform

00:37:19.640 --> 00:37:21.870
than Hindu in Mahayana
Buddhist iconography,

00:37:21.870 --> 00:37:23.970
which primarily owes to
the centuries of local

00:37:23.970 --> 00:37:25.750
artistic development within Angkor

00:37:25.750 --> 00:37:27.250
rather than just their import.

00:37:28.100 --> 00:37:30.380
It's also probable that
Buddhist terraces and converted

00:37:30.380 --> 00:37:33.370
temples were initially collectively
standardized in a layout

00:37:33.370 --> 00:37:36.270
and temple such as Preah
Palilay in Western present Thom

00:37:36.270 --> 00:37:38.038
thus may represent the first typed

00:37:38.038 --> 00:37:39.633
inversions found in Angkor.

00:37:39.633 --> 00:37:43.530
The ladders conversion, or at
least its new southern tower,

00:37:43.530 --> 00:37:45.680
based on the diagram here,

00:37:45.680 --> 00:37:47.300
has in fact been hypothesized

00:37:47.300 --> 00:37:48.790
to date from the late 13th century

00:37:48.790 --> 00:37:51.182
based on a radiometric analysis by Nara,

00:37:51.182 --> 00:37:54.463
who currently undertaking
anastylosis at the time.

00:37:55.340 --> 00:37:56.380
This was based,

00:37:56.380 --> 00:37:58.340
may have been based on
continued sacredness

00:37:58.340 --> 00:37:59.730
or scribed to the inner sanctuary

00:37:59.730 --> 00:38:01.570
in order to standardize these monuments,

00:38:01.570 --> 00:38:02.810
which is thought to have been converted

00:38:02.810 --> 00:38:04.870
into a reliquary in both cases.

00:38:04.870 --> 00:38:07.613
The placement of a Preah
Vihear fronting the temple

00:38:07.613 --> 00:38:10.270
and either the replication
or origin of this alignment

00:38:10.270 --> 00:38:12.400
between Buddhist terraces and reliquaries.

00:38:12.400 --> 00:38:15.530
It was just kind of a
chicken and egg situation.

00:38:15.530 --> 00:38:17.960
Especially through the
installation of the Preah Eintep

00:38:17.960 --> 00:38:20.210
reliquary shows that there was an attempt

00:38:20.210 --> 00:38:22.480
to create uniform
Angkorian Theravada space,

00:38:22.480 --> 00:38:23.780
regardless of the edifice.

00:38:26.140 --> 00:38:28.560
Also important to note with
these initial temple conversions

00:38:28.560 --> 00:38:30.700
were their confinement
to smaller structures,

00:38:30.700 --> 00:38:32.373
not the enormous state temples.

00:38:32.373 --> 00:38:34.570
These, if they were
transformed were subject

00:38:34.570 --> 00:38:36.090
to much larger renovations

00:38:36.090 --> 00:38:37.300
and either a blocking up

00:38:37.300 --> 00:38:40.320
or the overall demolition
of the Mount Meru towers.

00:38:40.320 --> 00:38:41.520
At least one of these temples,

00:38:41.520 --> 00:38:43.370
the 11th century Baphoun on the right

00:38:44.210 --> 00:38:46.450
was physically transformed
during the 15th century

00:38:46.450 --> 00:38:49.477
into a 65 meter statue
of a reclining Buddha

00:38:49.477 --> 00:38:52.470
at Theravada at the expense
of its central sanctuary,

00:38:52.470 --> 00:38:55.680
which is known from carbon
dates taken from iron crampons

00:38:55.680 --> 00:38:57.299
embedded within the Buddha.

00:38:57.299 --> 00:38:58.690
In a similar manner,

00:38:58.690 --> 00:39:01.230
Angkor's the first temple
mountain Phnom Bakheng

00:39:01.230 --> 00:39:04.120
was physically transformed into
a statue of a seated Buddha

00:39:04.120 --> 00:39:06.600
similarly through the
demolition of its towers.

00:39:06.600 --> 00:39:09.070
The research on this
installation is impossible

00:39:09.070 --> 00:39:11.460
as early French conservators
saw it as an eyesore

00:39:11.460 --> 00:39:12.840
and demolished it to reconstruct

00:39:12.840 --> 00:39:14.723
the original Mount Meru in the 1920s.

00:39:17.200 --> 00:39:19.090
And this image illustrates
it's also possible

00:39:19.090 --> 00:39:21.730
that many prah t-hat once
accessible were blocked up

00:39:21.730 --> 00:39:24.910
or transformed into closed
reliquaries during this period.

00:39:24.910 --> 00:39:28.040
Archival photographs show
that this was not a modern

00:39:28.040 --> 00:39:30.460
renovation in the red box here.

00:39:30.460 --> 00:39:32.630
The construction of reliquaries
and temple architecture,

00:39:32.630 --> 00:39:34.960
as well as the tempo
of temple conversions,

00:39:34.960 --> 00:39:36.870
moving from accessible to closed

00:39:36.870 --> 00:39:38.640
are ideas I hope to investigate in future

00:39:38.640 --> 00:39:40.610
expedition season at Angkor,

00:39:40.610 --> 00:39:42.420
as we create a better idea of when

00:39:42.420 --> 00:39:44.840
the central Hindu temple
space was not only abandoned,

00:39:44.840 --> 00:39:47.463
but seen as negligible or
even negatively charged.

00:39:49.060 --> 00:39:50.330
The placement of Buddhist terraces

00:39:50.330 --> 00:39:52.940
has thus far been proven
to be rarely arbitrary.

00:39:52.940 --> 00:39:55.840
As I previously indicated in
our excavations have on earth

00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:57.920
radiometric, artifactual structural

00:39:57.920 --> 00:39:59.219
and even votive remains associated

00:39:59.219 --> 00:40:01.030
with earlier domestic or religious

00:40:01.030 --> 00:40:02.840
dwellings on the same site.

00:40:02.840 --> 00:40:05.280
However, the most unique
patterns of Preah Vihear

00:40:05.280 --> 00:40:08.710
occur in relation to temples,
as well as arterial roads.

00:40:08.710 --> 00:40:10.300
Based on connections to these elements,

00:40:10.300 --> 00:40:11.360
I refer to these alignments

00:40:11.360 --> 00:40:14.040
as foci of memories of working hypothesis.

00:40:14.040 --> 00:40:15.740
Whereby memory refers to the continued

00:40:15.740 --> 00:40:16.950
significance and reverence

00:40:16.950 --> 00:40:18.600
for ancient things over time,

00:40:18.600 --> 00:40:21.090
and the reckoning of the past
the populations undertook

00:40:21.090 --> 00:40:22.610
when establishing their futures

00:40:22.610 --> 00:40:24.970
across multi temporal landscapes.

00:40:24.970 --> 00:40:26.010
Working with our data,

00:40:26.010 --> 00:40:29.360
I've established a few important
caveats for each focus.

00:40:29.360 --> 00:40:32.070
Each appears to honor and
re-legitimize or reify

00:40:32.070 --> 00:40:34.170
a Romano-Buddhist sanctuary

00:40:34.170 --> 00:40:36.030
within his place in the landscape.

00:40:36.030 --> 00:40:37.950
which in turn reinforced and legitimated

00:40:37.950 --> 00:40:39.720
the original layout of Angkor Thom,

00:40:39.720 --> 00:40:42.710
it's road ways and its
individual monuments.

00:40:42.710 --> 00:40:43.940
Renovations are also,

00:40:43.940 --> 00:40:46.226
and conversions are also common

00:40:46.226 --> 00:40:48.100
amongst temples that anchor foci.

00:40:48.100 --> 00:40:49.500
The key concept as well,

00:40:49.500 --> 00:40:52.189
number two is old infrastructure
in new Preah Vihear

00:40:52.189 --> 00:40:56.090
found with a niche focus embody
a reciprocal relationship

00:40:56.090 --> 00:40:58.240
were by neither is sacred within

00:40:59.654 --> 00:41:02.380
Theravada Buddhist
landscape without the other.

00:41:02.380 --> 00:41:04.040
Third, what is found in Angkor Thom

00:41:04.040 --> 00:41:06.700
is the culmination of each
focus and it is unknown

00:41:06.700 --> 00:41:10.230
whether these areas were developed
gradually or immediately.

00:41:10.230 --> 00:41:12.330
However, none of them,

00:41:12.330 --> 00:41:15.570
none of the foci are found
in any epigraphic records

00:41:15.570 --> 00:41:18.220
and are inferred through
analysis of map data,

00:41:18.220 --> 00:41:20.120
and thus the flexibility of this juristic

00:41:20.120 --> 00:41:21.930
enables additional interpretation.

00:41:21.930 --> 00:41:23.170
So this is just a hypothesis,

00:41:23.170 --> 00:41:26.970
but it seems to have
some spatial relevance.

00:41:26.970 --> 00:41:28.100
The Bayon for example,

00:41:28.100 --> 00:41:29.700
formed the focal point of the concentric

00:41:29.700 --> 00:41:32.660
layout of Buddhist terraces,
none of which are identical.

00:41:32.660 --> 00:41:35.010
This suggests that focus
was created gradually

00:41:35.010 --> 00:41:37.070
rather than as a single
act of construction.

00:41:37.070 --> 00:41:38.490
And that monasteries in the focus

00:41:38.490 --> 00:41:42.270
were not created by a single
faction, but several over time.

00:41:42.270 --> 00:41:44.420
Still by coincidence or by some continuous

00:41:44.420 --> 00:41:48.580
perception of the Bayon the
layout today resembles a mandola

00:41:48.580 --> 00:41:51.010
surrounding the temple and
clearly cements the Bayon

00:41:51.010 --> 00:41:52.960
as the continuous pivot of the citadel.

00:41:54.050 --> 00:41:57.191
Another examples found in the
form of a staggered line of

00:41:57.191 --> 00:41:59.060
Buddhist terraces spanning
the entire longitudinal

00:41:59.060 --> 00:42:00.730
thoroughfare of Angkor Thom.

00:42:00.730 --> 00:42:02.640
only interrupted by the central zone,

00:42:02.640 --> 00:42:03.910
which during survey we called

00:42:03.910 --> 00:42:06.320
the north south gate road zigzag.

00:42:06.320 --> 00:42:08.540
Interestingly, Zhou Daguan attributes

00:42:08.540 --> 00:42:09.950
some significance to at least

00:42:09.950 --> 00:42:12.420
the Southern portion of
this route in his writings.

00:42:12.420 --> 00:42:15.010
As you can see in the
quote in the bottom right

00:42:15.010 --> 00:42:16.480
This thoroughfare ultra features

00:42:16.480 --> 00:42:19.170
a large number of structures
with fire brick remains.

00:42:19.170 --> 00:42:22.580
Bricks interestingly had
not been used on mass

00:42:22.580 --> 00:42:25.240
in Angkorian architecture
since the late 10th

00:42:25.240 --> 00:42:26.073
or early 11th centuries,

00:42:26.073 --> 00:42:27.380
when they were replaced almost entirely

00:42:27.380 --> 00:42:29.930
by a combination of
sandstone and litreage.

00:42:29.930 --> 00:42:32.070
And it's therefore likely
bricks are re-introduced

00:42:32.070 --> 00:42:33.140
to Angkorian architecture

00:42:33.140 --> 00:42:35.280
by means of expanding Thai influence

00:42:35.280 --> 00:42:36.860
where brick and plaster construction

00:42:36.860 --> 00:42:38.770
during this period are abundant.

00:42:38.770 --> 00:42:40.780
Additionally, brick renovations appear

00:42:40.780 --> 00:42:42.730
on top of sandstone and litreage.

00:42:42.730 --> 00:42:45.460
So it's likely that this
was a later installation.

00:42:45.460 --> 00:42:47.540
We excavated one of the
structures along the route,

00:42:47.540 --> 00:42:49.660
and like other Preah
Vihear across the citadel,

00:42:49.660 --> 00:42:52.703
we did a bone deposit
near the central sanctuary

00:42:52.703 --> 00:42:54.411
to the 14th century.

00:42:54.411 --> 00:42:56.827
According to contemporary Thai sources,

00:42:56.827 --> 00:43:00.550
Angkor was successfully attacked
in 1431 by armies from the

00:43:00.550 --> 00:43:02.241
kingdom of Ayutthayan.

00:43:02.241 --> 00:43:03.640
Ayutthayan the Buddhist embodied

00:43:03.640 --> 00:43:05.450
the same rigid social hierarchy,

00:43:05.450 --> 00:43:07.490
standardized replication of architecture,

00:43:07.490 --> 00:43:08.860
divine rulership rights,

00:43:08.860 --> 00:43:11.250
and even the idea of
constructing a temple mountain

00:43:11.250 --> 00:43:12.270
at their island capital

00:43:12.270 --> 00:43:15.260
north of Bangkok as within Hindu Angkor,

00:43:15.260 --> 00:43:17.150
and the geopolitical
expansion of Ayutthaya

00:43:17.150 --> 00:43:19.210
between the 14th and 15th centuries,

00:43:19.210 --> 00:43:20.043
it's thought to have been

00:43:20.043 --> 00:43:21.930
a major cause of the
decommission of Angkor

00:43:21.930 --> 00:43:23.660
as the capital Cambodia.

00:43:23.660 --> 00:43:25.440
While Cambodia's ruling class

00:43:25.440 --> 00:43:27.170
left the region for a series of capitals

00:43:27.170 --> 00:43:28.340
surrounding modern Phnom Penh

00:43:28.340 --> 00:43:30.233
over the ensuing three centuries.

00:43:31.660 --> 00:43:34.060
Scholars such as Michael Vickery
highlight the possibility

00:43:34.060 --> 00:43:37.010
that Ayutthaya prince occupied Angkor Thom

00:43:37.010 --> 00:43:39.190
at some point during the mid 15th century,

00:43:39.190 --> 00:43:40.923
but for all intents and purposes,

00:43:41.824 --> 00:43:42.657
the old citadel was no longer

00:43:42.657 --> 00:43:45.200
a significant civic ceremonial center.

00:43:45.200 --> 00:43:46.610
Angkor too was now positioned

00:43:46.610 --> 00:43:49.010
squarely on Cambodia's frontier.

00:43:49.010 --> 00:43:51.810
Radiometric data found,
found across Angkor Thom,

00:43:51.810 --> 00:43:53.450
including from our own research,

00:43:53.450 --> 00:43:55.470
indicate the possibility of a 15th century

00:43:55.470 --> 00:43:57.160
upper limit of occupation.

00:43:57.160 --> 00:43:59.060
Angkor was taken from the Angkor Thom mode

00:43:59.060 --> 00:44:01.520
by Dan Penny's team from
the University of Sydney,

00:44:01.520 --> 00:44:04.550
suggest overall hydraulic
neglect during this period,

00:44:04.550 --> 00:44:06.700
which he describes as swamp like.

00:44:06.700 --> 00:44:08.630
Seriations of Chinese ceramics undertaken

00:44:08.630 --> 00:44:11.100
by Hiadara, David Brotherson and others,

00:44:11.100 --> 00:44:12.750
show an absence of Li dynasty

00:44:12.750 --> 00:44:14.640
that is late 14th and 15th century,

00:44:14.640 --> 00:44:18.050
blue and white Chinese export
wares at Preah Vihear sites,

00:44:18.050 --> 00:44:21.050
as opposed to Song dynasty
11th to 14th century,

00:44:21.050 --> 00:44:24.120
as well as Yuan dynasty,
(indistinct) and white wares,

00:44:24.120 --> 00:44:26.290
which indicate a relative
lack of habitational

00:44:26.290 --> 00:44:29.280
or votive activities
beyond the 15th century.

00:44:29.280 --> 00:44:31.510
The great temple of Angkor
Wat to the south meanwhile,

00:44:31.510 --> 00:44:34.340
was transformed into a prominent
Buddhist pilgrimage site

00:44:34.340 --> 00:44:36.370
during the 16th century.

00:44:36.370 --> 00:44:38.550
This conversion may have
in fact occurred earlier

00:44:38.550 --> 00:44:40.780
as two Buddhist terraces
had been constructed there,

00:44:40.780 --> 00:44:42.860
which according to
Cambodian world chronicles

00:44:42.860 --> 00:44:46.110
date from the years following
Angkor's defeat by Ayutthaya.

00:44:46.110 --> 00:44:47.760
Angkor Wat was originally constructed

00:44:47.760 --> 00:44:49.210
by King Suryavarman the second,

00:44:49.210 --> 00:44:52.250
during the early to mid 12th
century as a shrine to Vishnu,

00:44:52.250 --> 00:44:53.320
and holds the recognition

00:44:53.320 --> 00:44:56.010
as the world's largest religious monument.

00:44:56.010 --> 00:44:57.250
The temple is known especially

00:44:57.250 --> 00:45:00.490
for it's 1.6 kilometers
of release including an

00:45:00.490 --> 00:45:03.910
earlier illustration of the
churning of the ocean milk.

00:45:03.910 --> 00:45:06.110
And activity at the
temples documented in an

00:45:07.293 --> 00:45:08.550
expansive volume of inscriptions
in the Khmer language

00:45:08.550 --> 00:45:10.855
dating from 1546 CE onwards.

00:45:10.855 --> 00:45:13.570
And it was continuously
patronized by the royal family

00:45:13.570 --> 00:45:15.140
who walled up the old central sanctuary

00:45:15.140 --> 00:45:17.380
at the central most
tower with Buddha freezes

00:45:17.380 --> 00:45:19.870
decommissioning the earlier vision cellar.

00:45:19.870 --> 00:45:21.370
While a less destructive act from

00:45:21.370 --> 00:45:23.620
the Bakong or Pnohm
Bakheng re-envisioning,

00:45:23.620 --> 00:45:25.660
this blocking up of the
space clearly reflects

00:45:25.660 --> 00:45:28.500
similar perceptions of
earlier temple sanctuaries,

00:45:28.500 --> 00:45:30.490
as either defunct or dangerous.

00:45:30.490 --> 00:45:33.290
Inscriptions too clearly
engage with memory

00:45:33.290 --> 00:45:37.023
venerating the August ancestors
and Angkor's previous kings.

00:45:38.440 --> 00:45:41.760
To conclude, the landscape
of Buddhist terraces

00:45:41.760 --> 00:45:44.670
slash Preah Vihear illustrates
a unique and localized

00:45:44.670 --> 00:45:46.832
adoption of Theravada Buddhism

00:45:46.832 --> 00:45:48.550
in Angkor Thom and central Angkor.

00:45:48.550 --> 00:45:50.290
One which was required to negotiate

00:45:50.290 --> 00:45:52.430
the built environment of institutionalized

00:45:53.350 --> 00:45:54.183
political religious authority,

00:45:54.183 --> 00:45:56.080
but also propagate this
new religious practice

00:45:56.080 --> 00:45:59.410
in a unique framework, which
would guarantee its success.

00:45:59.410 --> 00:46:02.600
Theravada at Angkor I contend
was manifested nowhere else

00:46:02.600 --> 00:46:04.660
the same in Southeast Asia.

00:46:04.660 --> 00:46:06.660
The construction and placement
of these new structures

00:46:06.660 --> 00:46:09.260
honored earlier material and
spatial ritual traditions

00:46:09.260 --> 00:46:12.180
highlighting the importance
of core periphery relations

00:46:12.180 --> 00:46:14.670
and religious place-making
while also serving

00:46:14.670 --> 00:46:17.280
as an innovative advancement
with semantic Preah Vihear

00:46:17.280 --> 00:46:19.080
as familiar religious architectures.

00:46:19.940 --> 00:46:21.660
The incorporation of Hindu and Mahayana

00:46:21.660 --> 00:46:23.530
Buddhist infrastructure
into Theravada Buddhist

00:46:23.530 --> 00:46:27.180
understandings in place was
also indeed an evolving process,

00:46:27.180 --> 00:46:29.450
although more research is
necessary to understand

00:46:29.450 --> 00:46:31.720
any of these theoretical avenues.

00:46:31.720 --> 00:46:33.940
And finally Angkor Thom serves

00:46:33.940 --> 00:46:35.930
as a fascinating and important case study

00:46:35.930 --> 00:46:38.590
for religious transition in
the archeological record.

00:46:38.590 --> 00:46:41.300
One which unlike more prominent
civic ceremonial centers,

00:46:41.300 --> 00:46:43.710
such as Rome, Athens, or even Sukhothai,

00:46:43.710 --> 00:46:46.640
which was once itself a
town on the Khmer frontier,

00:46:46.640 --> 00:46:49.740
contains a relatively
underserved archeological record

00:46:49.740 --> 00:46:53.170
where the idealization of
history and search for origins

00:46:53.170 --> 00:46:54.820
did not come at the expense of the sites

00:46:54.820 --> 00:46:56.100
with more recent history,

00:46:56.100 --> 00:46:57.630
which is aside from that

00:46:57.630 --> 00:46:59.430
poor little Buddha of phnom Bakheng.

00:47:00.450 --> 00:47:03.130
Ideas of social memory,
indigenous use of time,

00:47:03.130 --> 00:47:04.880
continuity rather than the phasing

00:47:04.880 --> 00:47:06.720
and the apicalization of history

00:47:06.720 --> 00:47:08.880
and even modern perception
of these sacred sites

00:47:08.880 --> 00:47:10.690
by local worshipers can easily

00:47:10.690 --> 00:47:12.580
and accurately be analyzed here.

00:47:12.580 --> 00:47:14.080
With local collaboration,

00:47:14.080 --> 00:47:16.600
prioritization of Cambodian academic goals

00:47:16.600 --> 00:47:18.760
and honoring of Angkor's everlastingly

00:47:18.760 --> 00:47:20.140
spiritually charged nature,

00:47:20.140 --> 00:47:23.033
being paramount to all
successful future research.

00:47:24.180 --> 00:47:25.980
And these are just some of our goals

00:47:27.340 --> 00:47:28.173
for the upcoming two
field seasons in 2022,

00:47:28.173 --> 00:47:30.570
as well as one possibly in 2023.

00:47:30.570 --> 00:47:32.030
And I'd love to hear your questions.

00:47:32.030 --> 00:47:34.180
Again, it's been an honor
to present for all of you

00:47:34.180 --> 00:47:37.033
at Center for Southeast
Asian Studies, and thank you.

00:47:40.850 --> 00:47:42.070
- Thank you so much, Andrew.

00:47:42.070 --> 00:47:44.340
This is a really a rich presentation.

00:47:44.340 --> 00:47:47.860
I think we'll have a
lot of questions here.

00:47:47.860 --> 00:47:51.230
So what I'd like to do is
open it up to the audience.

00:47:51.230 --> 00:47:53.760
Andrew, maybe you can
stop the screen share,

00:47:53.760 --> 00:47:57.108
but we may ask you to
pull up some images later,

00:47:57.108 --> 00:47:58.478
but you seem to be pretty good

00:47:58.478 --> 00:47:59.311
at going back and forth between it,

00:47:59.311 --> 00:48:02.300
so we can see the faces of
people asking questions.

00:48:02.300 --> 00:48:03.960
So if anyone has a question

00:48:03.960 --> 00:48:07.640
I suggest you use the
