00:50:41.553 --> 00:50:43.940
you just can't say that.

00:50:43.940 --> 00:50:47.980
With Angkor what we're finding
in the archeological record

00:50:47.980 --> 00:50:52.300
is a discerning attempt to
create a worldview that makes

00:50:52.300 --> 00:50:55.730
sense to the people and
the hierarchies that exist.

00:50:55.730 --> 00:50:59.170
The idea that religious
dissemination is successful,

00:50:59.170 --> 00:51:00.470
not based on chaos,

00:51:00.470 --> 00:51:03.480
but based on continuity is
something that we're seeing

00:51:03.480 --> 00:51:05.960
within the Angkorian archeological record.

00:51:05.960 --> 00:51:08.094
The idea that sima,

00:51:08.094 --> 00:51:10.115
and these are few of the
things that I had to take out,

00:51:10.115 --> 00:51:11.030
otherwise the presentation
would've been hours,

00:51:11.030 --> 00:51:16.030
but the architecture itself
in many of the late 13th,

00:51:16.350 --> 00:51:19.640
early 14th century
structures is not recycled,

00:51:19.640 --> 00:51:20.473
it's quarried,

00:51:20.473 --> 00:51:23.140
and it's carved in a way
that almost is identical

00:51:23.140 --> 00:51:25.190
to the way that one would enter a temple.

00:51:26.116 --> 00:51:27.590
You see Buddhist terraces at Angkot Thom,

00:51:27.590 --> 00:51:30.090
with ballast rates and (murmurs)

00:51:30.090 --> 00:51:33.370
that are easily recognizable.

00:51:33.370 --> 00:51:36.540
You see the idea that
the sanctuary is always

00:51:36.540 --> 00:51:38.020
has it's face eastward,

00:51:38.020 --> 00:51:40.170
and the only time it
hadn't in Angkorian history

00:51:40.170 --> 00:51:42.770
was when the temple was
dedicated to Vishnu.

00:51:42.770 --> 00:51:47.510
And so there seems to be
this idea that Buddhism

00:51:47.510 --> 00:51:51.690
at Angkor is unique because
of not necessarily Hinduism,

00:51:51.690 --> 00:51:53.660
not necessarily what was practiced before

00:51:53.660 --> 00:51:56.833
in terms of religious
practice, but the space itself.

00:51:57.730 --> 00:52:01.010
The idea that this is what we
know as a place of worship.

00:52:01.010 --> 00:52:04.730
The Pratt is the temple,
it's not a question of,

00:52:05.794 --> 00:52:08.440
it's not a question of how

00:52:08.440 --> 00:52:09.690
are we going to include the temple,

00:52:09.690 --> 00:52:11.480
it's where does the temple go?

00:52:11.480 --> 00:52:13.930
It's not even a thought, it's
where does the temple go?

00:52:13.930 --> 00:52:15.710
And over time, as I mentioned,

00:52:15.710 --> 00:52:18.450
as Ayutthayan traditions become stronger

00:52:18.450 --> 00:52:21.190
and geopolitically become
more dominant in the region,

00:52:21.190 --> 00:52:23.546
you do see the shift towards

00:52:23.546 --> 00:52:25.320
a more Thai,

00:52:25.320 --> 00:52:26.760
not necessarily religious version,

00:52:26.760 --> 00:52:29.470
but material version of Buddhism,

00:52:29.470 --> 00:52:31.450
which is again, an incredibly
controversial point

00:52:31.450 --> 00:52:32.820
in the 20th and 21st century.

00:52:32.820 --> 00:52:36.586
But at the same time, there's a Cambodia,

00:52:36.586 --> 00:52:37.419
there is, you're right,

00:52:37.419 --> 00:52:39.310
a uniquely Cambodian tradition
and uniquely Thai tradition,

00:52:39.310 --> 00:52:42.300
which admittedly comes
mostly from the 20th century

00:52:42.300 --> 00:52:46.160
when the French essentially did not allow

00:52:46.160 --> 00:52:48.840
Cambodian monks to travel to Thailand.

00:52:48.840 --> 00:52:51.132
They said, you cannot
be indoctrinated here.

00:52:51.132 --> 00:52:51.965
We're going to create our own school.

00:52:51.965 --> 00:52:54.860
And this is the way to make
sure that our territory is

00:52:54.860 --> 00:52:57.050
consolidated within
Cambodia is create that.

00:52:57.050 --> 00:52:58.800
So there the tradition has been

00:52:58.800 --> 00:53:00.850
much more modern than ancient.

00:53:00.850 --> 00:53:03.940
And so, within early Theravada,

00:53:03.940 --> 00:53:06.370
it's much easier to tell a distinct,

00:53:06.370 --> 00:53:09.550
distinct different between
regions and what was adopted.

00:53:09.550 --> 00:53:12.300
And I think maybe that gives us somewhat,

00:53:12.300 --> 00:53:15.730
maybe that's a somewhat meandering
answer to your question,

00:53:15.730 --> 00:53:18.702
but I think I would stand
by the idea that this was,

00:53:18.702 --> 00:53:19.900
as I say, localized,

00:53:19.900 --> 00:53:23.693
based on what people
knew of religious space.

