And in terms of the
iconography, the iconoclasm,

00:55:52.460 --> 00:55:54.193
it was actually something that,

00:55:55.316 --> 00:55:57.060
when I was writing my
thesis I toyed around with,

00:55:57.060 --> 00:56:00.923
as an earlier re-envisioning
of the Angkorian landscape.

00:56:01.980 --> 00:56:05.070
Mahayana Buddhism was something
that was revolutionary

00:56:05.070 --> 00:56:08.310
and new and tied to a king,
maybe one or two iings.

00:56:08.310 --> 00:56:10.987
It's not quite clear whether
Jayavarman six ancenstor

00:56:10.987 --> 00:56:12.860
in Jayavarman the second
was a Mahayana Buddhist,

00:56:12.860 --> 00:56:17.860
but it was a sense that these
sanctuaries could be used,

00:56:17.900 --> 00:56:19.840
could be reinterpreted.

00:56:19.840 --> 00:56:22.730
All they needed was the
images gone, Jayavarman gone,

00:56:22.730 --> 00:56:25.260
and they were still
perfectly good sanctuaries.

00:56:25.260 --> 00:56:27.150
They still were recognizable.

00:56:27.150 --> 00:56:30.150
They were still oriented in a
way that was understandable.

00:56:30.150 --> 00:56:31.650
They still housed populations.

00:56:31.650 --> 00:56:33.090
They still housed laborers,

00:56:33.090 --> 00:56:37.420
and were the foci of all of
political and economic systems

00:56:37.420 --> 00:56:39.090
that they were before.

00:56:39.090 --> 00:56:41.170
So, it's an interesting,

00:56:41.170 --> 00:56:43.550
it's an interesting idea to say the least.

00:56:43.550 --> 00:56:44.383
And I think there,

00:56:44.383 --> 00:56:46.430
there actually has been
a good amount of work

00:56:47.370 --> 00:56:49.980
done on the architecture itself,

00:56:49.980 --> 00:56:54.680
but not necessarily on what
types of things iconoclasm

00:56:54.680 --> 00:56:56.725
and what types of asks,

00:56:56.725 --> 00:56:59.450
what happens when an image
gets hacked out of a temple

00:56:59.450 --> 00:57:00.807
or gets transformed?

00:57:00.807 --> 00:57:02.354
There were actually several that were,

00:57:02.354 --> 00:57:03.430
Buddhas were transformed into lingams

00:57:03.430 --> 00:57:05.440
and into rishi or saints.

00:57:05.440 --> 00:57:08.690
And so, what does that mean,

00:57:08.690 --> 00:57:10.030
and how do we,

00:57:10.030 --> 00:57:12.210
or how do we look more at that?

00:57:12.210 --> 00:57:15.280
Because the way that Angkorian
history is often constructed

00:57:15.280 --> 00:57:18.490
is that there's periods of
boom and bust continuously,

00:57:18.490 --> 00:57:19.940
boom and bust, boom and bust.

00:57:21.130 --> 00:57:22.300
And this one was a dramatic event.

00:57:22.300 --> 00:57:26.590
And every time a king returned
to some sort of royal cult,

00:57:26.590 --> 00:57:29.450
every single time there's always violence.

00:57:29.450 --> 00:57:31.350
There's always thought to be violence.

00:57:32.250 --> 00:57:35.260
Iconoclasm is a violent act in itself,

00:57:35.260 --> 00:57:37.840
but it's not clear from the 13th century,

00:57:37.840 --> 00:57:40.760
although Zhou Daguan mentions
a war with Sukhothai,

00:57:40.760 --> 00:57:45.460
that the Angkorian kingdom
was in any sort of tumult

00:57:45.460 --> 00:57:47.950
climatological issues aside.

00:57:47.950 --> 00:57:49.190
So, I would like to,

00:57:49.190 --> 00:57:50.870
I really would like to explore more

00:57:50.870 --> 00:57:53.420
about the iconoclasm of Hinduism.

00:57:53.420 --> 00:57:56.330
So it's, yeah,

00:57:56.330 --> 00:57:58.050
it's something to investigate further.

00:57:58.050 --> 00:58:00.210
I think I, again, again,

00:58:00.210 --> 00:58:02.260
another meandering answers your question.

00:58:04.160 --> 00:58:07.570
- Can I ask just a brief
technical follow-up question

00:58:07.570 --> 00:58:10.610
that may be obvious to all
the archeologists in the room,

00:58:10.610 --> 00:58:11.740
but how does when,

00:58:11.740 --> 00:58:15.100
I can understand how one
might deit existing objects,

00:58:15.100 --> 00:58:18.450
but how does when deit when
something was destroyed?

00:58:18.450 --> 00:58:21.080
Like for example, the hacking
away of a Buddha face,

00:58:21.080 --> 00:58:25.230
it removes the material so what kind of,

00:58:25.230 --> 00:58:27.000
how does one actually deit that?

00:58:27.000 --> 00:58:28.720
- They don't, and then
that's part of that's

00:58:28.720 --> 00:58:30.640
part of sort of, it adds up.

00:58:30.640 --> 00:58:32.553
And so deductive reasoning is used.

00:58:33.966 --> 00:58:35.583
There's two theories on the iconoclasm ,

00:58:35.583 --> 00:58:36.663
one, that it occurred during

00:58:36.663 --> 00:58:38.201
the reign of Jayavarman the eighth,

00:58:38.201 --> 00:58:40.490
and the second is in a sort
of newer reaction is that

00:58:40.490 --> 00:58:45.110
it occurred during the
reign of Peramesvarapada,

00:58:45.110 --> 00:58:47.220
who was the last Hindu king.

00:58:47.220 --> 00:58:49.520
And according to the
Cambodian real chronicles,

00:58:49.520 --> 00:58:51.500
he was in fact assassinated
by his gardener.

00:58:51.500 --> 00:58:54.210
So there was Theravada
Buddhist kings after that.

00:58:54.210 --> 00:58:56.873
So those are kind of the two ideas.

00:58:58.343 --> 00:59:01.570
And through archeology unless
there's residue on an act,

00:59:01.570 --> 00:59:02.700
you really can't do it.

00:59:02.700 --> 00:59:04.820
It's all, it's all speculative.

00:59:04.820 --> 00:59:07.243
You have to hope more epigraphy comes up.

00:59:10.700 --> 00:59:12.500
- I see a hand up from Ward Keeler,

00:59:12.500 --> 00:59:14.580
and Ben has appeared on video.

00:59:14.580 --> 00:59:16.680
So I'll call on Ward Keeler first,

00:59:16.680 --> 00:59:18.460
and then turned to Ben after that,

00:59:18.460 --> 00:59:19.810
go ahead Ward.

00:59:19.810 --> 00:59:23.530
- Thanks, I work in Burma and Indonesia.

00:59:23.530 --> 00:59:25.993
So Cambodia is really
quite a foreign to me,

00:59:27.013 --> 00:59:30.610
but I wonder if a pattern
that seems discernible

00:59:30.610 --> 00:59:34.210
all over Southeast Asia
doesn't help your explanation.

00:59:34.210 --> 00:59:36.750
That is to say that any site

00:59:36.750 --> 00:59:41.750
can be seen to be a residue
of enormous amounts of power,

00:59:44.167 --> 00:59:46.190
of spiritual power,
whatever you wanna call it.

00:59:46.190 --> 00:59:48.440
It's just, there's a note of power there

00:59:48.440 --> 00:59:50.890
that is available to be tapped.

00:59:50.890 --> 00:59:54.964
So, of course you would
wanna keep the place because

00:59:54.964 --> 00:59:57.010
the places are imbued
with that kind of power.

00:59:57.010 --> 00:59:58.210
At the same time,

00:59:58.210 --> 01:00:02.210
every religious reform movement is a way

01:00:02.210 --> 01:00:04.640
for those in power

01:00:05.999 --> 01:00:08.890
to divert more power to themselves,

01:00:08.890 --> 01:00:10.720
to make a break with the past,

01:00:10.720 --> 01:00:14.220
to show some sort of new
direction that enables them

01:00:14.220 --> 01:00:15.400
to do things like, you know,

01:00:15.400 --> 01:00:17.710
what happens in Burmese history is that,

01:00:17.710 --> 01:00:21.807
all the monks have to be re-initiated,

01:00:22.930 --> 01:00:26.690
which means a completely
new order to the hierarchy.

01:00:26.690 --> 01:00:30.540
So, I just wonder if that
makes sense as a way of putting

01:00:30.540 --> 01:00:34.260
together the different parts
of what you have described?

01:00:34.260 --> 01:00:36.410
- Fully, yeah, a hundred
percent and that's,

01:00:36.410 --> 01:00:38.960
that's what's missing from
the equation is really

01:00:38.960 --> 01:00:41.750
any royal record of
what's going on at Angkor.

01:00:41.750 --> 01:00:44.730
You don't know why Theravada
Buddhism sneaked in.

01:00:44.730 --> 01:00:47.524
People have painted it
as a social revolution,

01:00:47.524 --> 01:00:48.843
which is something that I have disputed.

01:00:50.283 --> 01:00:54.290
And it's the continuity we see
in the archeological record,

01:00:54.290 --> 01:00:58.130
indeed reflect the idea
that power is consolidated

01:00:58.130 --> 01:00:59.320
and spaces remain sacred.

01:00:59.320 --> 01:01:00.600
Again, why,

01:01:00.600 --> 01:01:02.410
why not build something familiar

01:01:02.410 --> 01:01:04.500
if you're working with familiar power?

01:01:04.500 --> 01:01:05.983
So I fully agree with that.

01:01:08.780 --> 01:01:11.230
- Andrew, thanks very much
for a very informative

01:01:12.758 --> 01:01:15.340
and fascinating and
revealing presentation.

01:01:15.340 --> 01:01:18.770
A lot of it was new to me
and I learned a lot from it.

01:01:18.770 --> 01:01:23.080
I wonder if you would agree
that we're talking about a major

01:01:23.080 --> 01:01:25.933
transformation in Cambodian society here,

01:01:27.060 --> 01:01:29.230
not just a religious transformation,

01:01:29.230 --> 01:01:32.450
but political and social transformation

01:01:32.450 --> 01:01:35.913
as well in the 14th and 15th centuries,

01:01:38.638 --> 01:01:40.400
and I wonder if you'd like to comment

01:01:40.400 --> 01:01:43.330
on some of the traditional explanations

01:01:43.330 --> 01:01:46.740
for that transformation
or those transformations

01:01:48.115 --> 01:01:51.370
and how your explanation
and your observations

01:01:51.370 --> 01:01:55.020
fit in to the sort of more longstanding

01:01:55.020 --> 01:01:57.970
or traditional explanations.

01:01:57.970 --> 01:02:00.490
You know, one of them that played around

01:02:01.893 --> 01:02:04.862
for a long time is that
Jayavarman the seventh,

01:02:04.862 --> 01:02:08.320
who built Angkor Thom
with his 40 year reign

01:02:09.948 --> 01:02:11.030
and massive building program,

01:02:11.030 --> 01:02:12.080
just (murmurs) source

01:02:13.317 --> 01:02:16.571
to the Cambodian population and led to,

01:02:16.571 --> 01:02:20.460
a major change in the popular

01:02:21.320 --> 01:02:24.053
image of centralized,

01:02:25.714 --> 01:02:27.147
centralized empire and kingdom,

01:02:27.147 --> 01:02:29.940
and moved to a more village oriented

01:02:31.028 --> 01:02:33.260
Theravada Buddhist society away

01:02:33.260 --> 01:02:38.260
from a Hindu and Mahayana
Buddhist society.

01:02:38.280 --> 01:02:40.470
But there are two other

01:02:40.470 --> 01:02:42.663
more recent explanations which might,

01:02:44.040 --> 01:02:47.160
I'd be interested to
hear your comments on.

01:02:47.160 --> 01:02:51.008
One of them is that it was a change

01:02:51.008 --> 01:02:53.060
in the world trade patterns

01:02:54.335 --> 01:02:58.257
that the world trade going
past the south China sea,

01:02:59.440 --> 01:03:04.280
made the option very attractive
for the Angkorian elites

01:03:04.280 --> 01:03:06.780
to move further south down the river,

01:03:06.780 --> 01:03:10.450
to be closer to the south China sea trade.

01:03:10.450 --> 01:03:14.793
And Angkor was abandoned basically for an,

01:03:15.720 --> 01:03:17.390
an inland agrarian society had changed

01:03:17.390 --> 01:03:20.890
to a maritime commercial society.

01:03:20.890 --> 01:03:25.150
And that might be something
that the Theravada Buddhism

01:03:25.150 --> 01:03:27.900
and its adoption broadly across Cambodia

01:03:27.900 --> 01:03:32.087
had something to do with,
that economic change.

01:03:32.087 --> 01:03:33.410
- Yeah.
- And then

01:03:33.410 --> 01:03:37.830
we have the climate explanation as well.

01:03:37.830 --> 01:03:42.502
The 1300s where basically

01:03:42.502 --> 01:03:46.410
the end of the medieval warm period,

01:03:46.410 --> 01:03:49.510
it became much less wet,

01:03:49.510 --> 01:03:53.180
a lot drier and more frequent
droughts in the 1300s

01:03:54.771 --> 01:03:55.604
and early 1400s.

01:03:55.604 --> 01:03:57.840
Does that have anything to
do with the transformation

01:03:57.840 --> 01:04:00.263
that you're talking about?

01:04:01.340 --> 01:04:03.930
And finally, just a quick question related

01:04:03.930 --> 01:04:05.600
to what you're talking about.

01:04:05.600 --> 01:04:09.580
I just wonder whether the dominance

01:04:09.580 --> 01:04:14.123
in Jayavarman the seventh's
reign of Mahayana Buddhism,

01:04:15.350 --> 01:04:17.550
which was unusual for compared

01:04:17.550 --> 01:04:19.480
to previous Angkorian monarchs,

01:04:19.480 --> 01:04:24.240
even though Mahayana Buddhism
was part of the religious

01:04:24.240 --> 01:04:26.460
structure along with Hinduism.

01:04:26.460 --> 01:04:30.270
But the unusual predominance
of Mahayana Buddhism,

01:04:30.270 --> 01:04:34.100
was that in a way a kind
of transitional phase

01:04:34.100 --> 01:04:38.625
towards a new kind of Theravada Buddhism,

01:04:38.625 --> 01:04:42.787
and a Theravada Buddhist
transition that was made possible

01:04:44.470 --> 01:04:48.850
rather than precipitated as
another explanation might have

01:04:48.850 --> 01:04:52.183
it by, by Jayavarman the seventh's reign.

01:04:53.810 --> 01:04:57.373
- So, as we know in the
1300s, in the 1200s,

01:04:58.531 --> 01:04:59.910
right after the death of
Jayavarman the seventh,

01:04:59.910 --> 01:05:04.189
Angkor got rocked by event
after event, after event.

01:05:04.189 --> 01:05:07.780
First, mega monsoons and mega droughts

01:05:07.780 --> 01:05:10.160
almost are believed to
have begun to decimate

01:05:10.160 --> 01:05:13.250
the hydrology of Angkorians
and greater Angkor

01:05:13.250 --> 01:05:15.520
most notably during that period.

01:05:15.520 --> 01:05:20.520
Then you have the hypothesis
of the population of a plague

01:05:22.190 --> 01:05:24.260
just of expansion from other qualities,

01:05:24.260 --> 01:05:26.520
Sukhothai and Ayutthaya,

01:05:29.690 --> 01:05:32.253
successively expanded during this period.

01:05:34.130 --> 01:05:36.070
So, in terms of Theravada Buddhism,

01:05:36.070 --> 01:05:39.180
even though these things
seem to correlate Jayavarman

01:05:39.180 --> 01:05:41.600
exploited the resources of the capital.

01:05:41.600 --> 01:05:45.010
As Lawrence Briggs wrote,

01:05:45.010 --> 01:05:48.170
the Khmer got leaked by religion

01:05:48.170 --> 01:05:50.440
or something that (murmurs) quote.

01:05:50.440 --> 01:05:55.440
But it's very, it's very hard
and just not wise quite yet

01:05:57.145 --> 01:05:58.510
to connect Theravada Buddhism

01:05:58.510 --> 01:06:02.700
and any sort of social
upheaval to those events.

01:06:02.700 --> 01:06:04.870
They seem to make sense.

01:06:04.870 --> 01:06:07.810
But again, I'd like to see,
I just, as an archeologist,

01:06:07.810 --> 01:06:11.140
I'd like to see the connection
between monastic construction

01:06:11.140 --> 01:06:13.880
and any type of climatological fluctuation

01:06:15.120 --> 01:06:16.630
in more than just,

01:06:16.630 --> 01:06:18.240
more than just circumstantial events

01:06:18.240 --> 01:06:19.190
happening around the same time.

01:06:19.190 --> 01:06:20.829
It's means it's,

01:06:20.829 --> 01:06:23.060
it's a very logical
explanation, but again,

01:06:23.060 --> 01:06:26.260
dangerous, without more
evidence on my part, at least.

01:06:26.260 --> 01:06:27.593
In terms of trade,

01:06:29.620 --> 01:06:31.470
there was, I mean,

01:06:31.470 --> 01:06:35.760
there's theories that the
focus moved to the Mekong Delta

01:06:35.760 --> 01:06:39.417
before the traditional
sacrum of Angkor before.

01:06:39.417 --> 01:06:42.620
I mean, it was a logical place
based on the trade wealth

01:06:42.620 --> 01:06:44.430
in the south China sea that was coming in.

01:06:44.430 --> 01:06:46.910
And I mentioned, as I mentioned,

01:06:46.910 --> 01:06:49.650
we do have evidence of an
upper limit potentially

01:06:49.650 --> 01:06:51.140
at Buddhist terraces at Angkor Thom,

01:06:51.140 --> 01:06:53.780
based on those Chinese ceramic seriations.

01:06:53.780 --> 01:06:56.180
The idea that there have not
