01:09:27.970 --> 01:09:29.370
with the basis of stupa.

01:09:29.370 --> 01:09:31.420
So they may have been considered

01:09:31.420 --> 01:09:33.070
luxury goods in that perspective.

01:09:36.222 --> 01:09:40.630
- The production of cupboard
boxes like that goes back

01:09:40.630 --> 01:09:44.810
to a point earlier than
the date you've been giving

01:09:44.810 --> 01:09:46.833
for the introduction of Theravada,

01:09:47.700 --> 01:09:48.890
by several centuries.

01:09:48.890 --> 01:09:53.890
And so, I'm wondering whether
this is a very micro scale

01:09:55.140 --> 01:09:59.680
example of how production of a
certain kind of object within

01:09:59.680 --> 01:10:01.500
the Angkorian material culture

01:10:04.033 --> 01:10:05.890
could be shifted in use from

01:10:06.800 --> 01:10:11.800
some kind of offering
equipment for a Hindu context

01:10:11.800 --> 01:10:15.053
into a Theravada Buddhist context?

01:10:16.200 --> 01:10:19.900
- Sure, I was actually
thinking about this one

01:10:19.900 --> 01:10:22.470
right after we excavated the boxes.

01:10:22.470 --> 01:10:25.040
And there's kind of two
ways you can think about it.

01:10:25.040 --> 01:10:29.150
The first is that those boxes
were considered ancient goods

01:10:29.150 --> 01:10:33.222
and were considered and were
given as (murmurs) of deposits,

01:10:33.222 --> 01:10:35.460
and then thus are kind of anachronistic.

01:10:35.460 --> 01:10:40.100
The other is that they
were from an earlier

01:10:40.100 --> 01:10:42.263
era of occupation on the same site.

01:10:43.649 --> 01:10:45.493
On three of the four
sites that we excavated,

01:10:46.480 --> 01:10:49.080
we found ceramic offerings or not,

01:10:49.080 --> 01:10:49.970
sorry not ceramic offerings,

01:10:49.970 --> 01:10:52.040
ceramic remains that dated from

01:10:52.040 --> 01:10:54.130
an earlier period as sort of related

01:10:54.130 --> 01:10:57.309
to the strategic graphy
of our radiocarbon dates.

01:10:57.309 --> 01:10:59.870
And so there is a thought
that at least in one of,

01:10:59.870 --> 01:11:00.990
at least with the site,

01:11:00.990 --> 01:11:03.560
with the gypsum foundation stone we found,

01:11:03.560 --> 01:11:06.120
which was actually surrounded
by bones and charcoal,

01:11:06.120 --> 01:11:08.030
that you might have

01:11:08.030 --> 01:11:11.010
the site of an earlier
religious occupation.

01:11:11.010 --> 01:11:12.250
And then a,

01:11:12.250 --> 01:11:14.618
that gives you more of why they may

01:11:14.618 --> 01:11:15.990
have constructed the Buddhist
terrace where they did,

01:11:15.990 --> 01:11:18.943
and b, you have

01:11:18.943 --> 01:11:21.330
some context that's actually

01:11:21.330 --> 01:11:23.940
temporarily appropriate
to where you find the box,

01:11:23.940 --> 01:11:26.057
and it doesn't necessarily
throw things out of whack.

01:11:26.057 --> 01:11:26.986
- Yeah.

01:11:26.986 --> 01:11:27.819
- Okay.
- Again,

01:11:27.819 --> 01:11:29.050
this is something to validate with more,

01:11:29.050 --> 01:11:31.320
with more field work I think.

01:11:31.320 --> 01:11:32.420
- Yes, please,

01:11:33.380 --> 01:11:34.654
please do.

01:11:34.654 --> 01:11:35.487
(all chuckling)

01:11:35.487 --> 01:11:36.320
- I appreciate it.

01:11:38.880 --> 01:11:40.560
